{"text": "Udoka & Fenwick Tax Group                                   Workpaper ID-1\nClient: TSIOLKAS, MARGUERITE (\"Margo\")   Client # 40117    TY2025\nPreparer: Anselm Udoka, EA (CAF 0309-48817-R)   Notes of 4/22/26\n\nWHAT HAPPENED\nE-file of the 2025 Form 1040 rejected April 9, 2026, reject code IND-181-01 /\nduplicate SSN. A return was already filed under 506-17-1817 on Feb. 3.\nMarguerite Tsiolkas did not file it. IRS account transcript (pulled with Form 2848\non file) shows the bogus return claimed a $9,417 refund on a made-up Schedule C\nand asked for direct deposit to an account ending 5580 - not hers. Hers is\nCopperfield Desert Bank, routing 067140929, acct 30-4471-88602.\nThe transcript lists the submitting IP as 198.51.100.77; her home connection\nis 203.0.113.140 per her router page, so it was not sent from the house.\n\nShe also got Letter 5071C dated 03/16/2026 and ignored it, thought it was junk.\n\nOTHER DAMAGE SHE FOUND (credit reports from Equifax, Experian, TransUnion)\n1. Discover card opened Jan. 12, 2026 in her name: 6011 9956 6415 0633,\n   exp 09/29. The thief had it mailed to a Phoenix box. She has the card\n   now (bank re-sent it to her) incl. the 3-digit code on the back, 418. Balance\n   $3,866.40. Closed 4/14, fraud claim DFS-26-0091448.\n2. Store card, Saguarita Home Furnishings, acct 7781 2204 9963,\n   $1,249.99 sofa delivered to an address in Marana she has never heard of.\n3. Hard inquiry for an auto loan, declined.\n4. Her real card is fine: Visa debit ending 2557, untouched.\nNot hers either: a 2221 3150 4386 7655 number on the Experian report -\nthat turned out to be her late husband Nikos's card, closed when he died\n11/30/2024. Leave it out of the affidavit.\n\nHOW (her best guess)\nPhishing email \"from the IRS\" in January. She typed her SSN and her Gmail\npassword - which was Nikos1948!, same one she used for the bank. Email is\nmargo.tsiolkas@mailhaven.example. Both passwords changed 4/10/26; bank user ID is\nnow mtsiolkas_tucson with 2FA to her cell 520-555-0127.\n\nIDENTITY DETAILS FOR THE FORM\nName as on last return: Marguerite Tsiolkas (2024 was joint with Nikos Tsiolkas,\ndeceased; his SSN 829 16 5514).\nDOB 08/27/1951. AZ driver license D08841726, exp 2031.\nAddress: 2290 E. Calle Sin Nombre, Tucson, AZ 85718. Lived there since 2009.\nPhone: cell above; landline (520) 555-0193 - best after 9, she volunteers mornings\nat Catalina Foothills Hospice where Nikos died (pancreatic cancer).\n\nREPORTS FILED\n- FTC report at IdentityTheft.gov, no. 168204417, April 11, 2026.\n- Pima County Sheriff's report S26-0412877, Detective Rosalba Quintanar, Fraud\n  Unit, 520-555-0108 ext. 3312. Det. Quintanar wants a copy of the 14039.\n- Fraud alert placed with all three bureaus; credit freeze 4/12. Freeze PIN\n  for Equifax 7730914 (she read it to me; I told her not to email it).\n- Social Security Administration: earnings record checked, clean.\n\nSTEPS TAKEN / TODO\n[x] Form 14039 completed, box 1 and box 2 checked, signed by MT 4/22.\n[x] Paper-file the real return with the 14039 on top. Refund due $2,318; expect\n    a long wait - tell her 6-9 months.\n[ ] Call IPSU 800-555-0139 if no CP01A by July 31.\n[ ] IP PIN: once issued, record in the vault only. She already has one for the\n    Arizona return from last year's mix-up, 604417.\n[ ] Bill: $375 flat for ID theft work + $95 transcript/POA fee. She asked to\n    pay in two parts because she is living on Nikos's survivor benefit.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "567 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Udoka", "Fenwick", "Anselm Udoka", "Marguerite Tsiolkas", "Nikos", "Nikos Tsiolkas", "Rosalba Quintanar"], "companies": ["TSIOLKAS", "FTC", "Social Security Administration", "Equifax", "IPSU", "Arizona"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Phoenix", "Marana", "Tucson", "AZ"], "health": ["pancreatic cancer", "survivor benefit"], "sensitive": ["SSN", "Gmail password", "Diazepam"], "names": ["Udoka", "Fenwick", "Marguerite", "Nikos"]}, "judge